        "explanation": "\\(f'(x)=-3\\\\cos^2x\\\\sin x\\). For \\(x\\\\in(0,\\\\pi)\\), the derivative is nonpositive and is negative except at isolated points, so \\(\\\\cos^3x\\) is strictly decreasing on \\([0,\\\\pi]\\).",
